<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Shizong of Jin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1123–1189</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Wanyan Yong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Shizong of Jin, Wanyan Yong, reigned over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a> from 1161 to 1189 after the overthrow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wanyan-liang">Prince Hailing</a>. He made peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> in 1165 and promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> language and traditions while Confucian learning flourished. His long, stable reign is regarded as the high point of the dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-shizong-of-jin.jpg" alt="Emperor Shizong of Jin" width="297" height="492" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 陳世倌 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%81%96%E5%B8%9D%E6%98%8E%E7%8E%8B%E5%96%84%E7%AB%AF%E9%8C%84%EF%BC%88%E5%AE%8B%E5%85%83%E6%98%8E%EF%BC%89_%E5%86%8A_%E9%87%91%E4%B8%96%E5%AE%97_K2A003132N000000011PAB_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
